    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0411" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72113/447</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Swiss Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sulzer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d352-f1"/>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 129</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>With regard to your memorandum of October 31 last,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d352-f2"
                    /> transmitting the inquiry of the German Government concerning patents, I have
                        <pb facs="0412" n="328" xml:id="pg328"/> the honor to enclose for your
                    information copy of a statement received from the Chairman of the Federal Trade
                    Commission on November 2, with reference to the application of the Trading with
                    the Enemy Act to the use by American citizens and corporations of patents and
                    copyrights owned or controlled by enemies or allies of enemy.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d352-a1.xml" xpointer="d352-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
